    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "The conjecture has been proven in the case when X is a general Wehler N-fold i.e. a general hypersurface of multidegree (2,··· ,2) in (P1)N+1 for N ≥ 3 ([CO15, Theorem 1.3]). In [FLT23], the structure of the boundary of the pesudoeﬀective cone Eﬀ(X) has been studied. The divergent–recurrent decomposition of ∂Eﬀ(X) is proven in [FLT23, Theorem 2.4.2], and the following result on the asymptotic behavior of volume function near ∂Eﬀ(X) is derived:"
