    "font" : "CMTI10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "Theorem 1.0.2 ([FLT23, Theorem 1.3.7]) Suppose X is a general Wehler Calabi-Yau N-fold. Then, for every pseudoeﬀective R-divisor D in ∂Eﬀ(X) and suﬃciently ample divisor A, there exists an integer s(D) ∈ {0,··· ,N − 2} and a real number δ(D) ∈ [1, 21(N − s(D))] such that"
